<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65582" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέδιμν-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			7.187
		</span></i>, etc.; ἡ, only v.l. in
		<i><span class="en">
			Id.
			1.192
		</span></i>:—a corn-measure, <i><span class="en">
			Hes.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			160.3
		</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. Ἀττικός, Σικελικός</span>,
			<i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.192
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Plb.
			2.15.1
		</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιτηρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1013.27
				</span></i>
			; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῖτον] κατὰ μέδιμνον συνωνούμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					22.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεδίμνῳ ἀπομετρήσασθαι ἀργύριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					3.2.27
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ γὰρ νόμος . . κωλύει παιδὶ μὴ
				ἐξεῖναι συμβάλλειν μηδὲ γυναικὶ πέρα μεδίμνου
			κριθῶν</span> to make a contract for value exceeding <i>a
				medimnus</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				10.10
			</span></i>: hence, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ κύριος ὑπὲρ μέδιμνόν
				ἐστ᾽ ἀνὴρ οὐδεὶς ἔτι</span>, i. e. he is no better
			than a woman, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				1025
			</span></i>, cf. Sch.ad loc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἁλῶν
			μ.</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλς</span>
			 (A). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Magna
			Graecia, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρουνός</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>, <i>pipe of a fountain</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				12.10
			</span></i>.</div>
